  "id": "398b19b4-93f3-43d2-8f99-948bf46d1ca3",
  "title": "SignSeek and A Reverse Sign Language Dictionary: Bridging the Gap in Open-Vocabulary Sign Recognition",
  "summary": "SignSeek introduces a saliency-guided articulator masking framework to overcome the challenge of automatic sign dictionary retrieval, achieving zero-shot generalisation to unseen BSL. The reverse sign language dictionary approach leverages free-form procedural descriptions to enable open-vocabulary sign recognition from continuous signing without gloss supervision.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "SignSeek closes the gap in cross-corpus retrieval on ASL-Citizen, WLASL, and NMFs-CSL without any downstream fine-tuning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The system achieves zero-shot generalisation to an entirely unseen British Sign Language (BSL), surpassing methods explicitly trained on BSL.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reverse sign language dictionary uses free-form procedural descriptions and a multilingual sentence encoder to enable open-vocabulary sign lookup.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
